<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18428" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluctŭōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		fluctus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of waves</i>, <i>billowy</i>
			(very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in mari fluctuoso,</span>”
				i. e. <i>stormy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Rud. 4, 2, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>with wave-like
				streaks</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">smaragdi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 5, 18, § 71</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
